selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py: probe for the session's app before sleeping

A new session for an already running process ("app": "<pid>") looks for
that pid on the a11y registry in a loop that sleeps one second *before*
every probe. Every session creation therefore takes at least one second and
is quantised to whole seconds, even when the application registered on the
bus long before. The E2E suite creates one session per krema start (82 per
run): about 87 s of a ~320 s run was this sleep.

Probe first and sleep 0.1 s between probes. The deadline (twice the
implicit timeout), the error on timeout and the per-probe work are
unchanged; a registry walk over a handful of applications every 100 ms does
not load the bus.

--- a/selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py
+++ b/selenium-webdriver-at-spi.py
@@ -206,8 +206,7 @@ class Session:
         def on_launched(context, info, platform_data):
             self.pid = platform_data['pid']
 
-            while datetime.now() < end_time:
-                time.sleep(1) # do not overwhelm the bus with queries, wait a bit
+            while True:
                 for desktop_index in range(pyatspi.Registry.getDesktopCount()):
                     desktop = pyatspi.Registry.getDesktop(desktop_index)
                     for app in desktop:
@@ -220,8 +219,9 @@ class Session:
                             continue
                     if self.browsing_context:
                         break
-                if self.browsing_context:
+                if self.browsing_context or datetime.now() >= end_time:
                     break
+                time.sleep(0.1) # do not overwhelm the bus with queries, wait a bit
             if not self.browsing_context:
                 raise RuntimeError('Failed to find application on a11y bus within time limit! It either crashed, or was too slow to start, or is stuck.')
 
